        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cut and uncut voided silk velvet with a gold ground. The pattern is a point repeat (i.e. symmetrical about a vertical axis), comprising compartments topped with coronets from which curvaceous foliage and flowers scroll and above which sits a sun motif. The length comprises three full repeats of the pattern which does not repeat widthwise. The selvedges are primarily gold but seem to have a green stripe. The glitter of the gold is still apparent."@en ;
